  "$Comment": "The Gravekeeper's look, every piece of it the game's own: an old, pale man on the player's own body, with grey hair, bushy grey brows and a grey chin-curtain beard under a dark wide-brimmed hat, a worn black long coat over a grey shirt, dark leather trousers, black work boots and brown work gloves. Parent Player brings the body, its animations and its hitbox; the role puts the shovel in his right hand and the lantern in his left. GradientSet and GradientId at the top tint the body's skin, and the face, ears and mouth carry the same pair so they match it. DefaultAttachments replaces the parent's list whole, so the face, ears, mouth, eyes and brows are listed again here. A greyscale texture takes its colour from GradientSet and GradientId, the dyes the character creator offers players: change a GradientId to re-dye one piece. The hair is the creator's generic medium cut, the one it puts under a hat brim. Light is his lantern's glow, a model light that moves with him; each hex digit is a red, green or blue level from 0 to f.",
